#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/ptodsl/rng/index.rst:22
msgid ""
"Each SIMT thread creates its own instance with a unique (seed, seq) pair. "
"The seed and initial 128-bit counter are immutable. The caller owns a "
"logical draw index and threads it through each method explicitly, so PTODSL "
"can carry the ordinary Python SSA name through runtime control flow. "
"``rand()`` returns a uint32; ``rand_uniform()`` returns float32 in [0, 1); "
"``rand_normal()`` uses the same cached Box-Muller construction as the "
"AscendC backend."
msgstr ""

